---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';

/**
 * Who publishes UnityIDE, and where it legitimately comes from.
 *
 * Written for two readers at once. The first is an ordinary visitor deciding
 * whether to trust a desktop binary from a site they have not heard of. The
 * second is a Google Ads policy reviewer assessing the "free desktop software"
 * certification, which exists precisely to establish that an advertiser is the
 * AUTHORITATIVE DISTRIBUTION SOURCE for what it advertises.
 *
 * Before this page the site never said who published it: no entity, no
 * location, no contact outside the two legal pages. A reviewer asking "is this
 * the real publisher, or someone redistributing someone else's binary?" had
 * nothing on the site to answer with — the single weakest point in the
 * application, and the reason this page exists.
 *
 * The "Official distribution" section is the load-bearing one. Naming the only
 * canonical hosts, and stating plainly that nothing is bundled, is what the
 * policy actually asks a publisher to assert. Keep the download URLs pointing
 * at the stable `latest` paths — a broken link here reads as an abandoned or
 * impersonated site, which is worse than having no page at all.
 */
---

<LegalLayout
  title="About UnityIDE"
  description="Who builds UnityIDE, and where to download it from safely."
>
  <p>
    UnityIDE is a dedicated IDE for Unity development, combining C# editing,
    Unity asset workflows, and AI assistance connected to your running Unity Editor.
  </p>

  <h2>Who publishes it</h2>
  <p>
    UnityIDE is developed and distributed by <strong>Unity IDE</strong>, based in
    India. We are an independent software publisher. UnityIDE is our own product —
    we develop it and distribute the official releases.
  </p>
  <p>
    Reach us at <a href="mailto:support@unityide.app">support@unityide.app</a> for
    support, security reports, press, or anything about the data we hold.
  </p>

  <h2>Official distribution</h2>
  <p>
    Updater signature verification is separate from operating-system publisher signing.
    The Windows installer is not yet publisher-signed, and the Apple Silicon macOS
    build is ad-hoc signed and marked Beta. See the
    <a href="/docs/getting-started/installation/">installation guide</a> for current
    requirements and platform-specific instructions.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong><a href="https://unityide.app">unityide.app</a> is the only official
    source for UnityIDE.</strong> Every genuine build is served from our own domain:
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Platform</th><th>Official download</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Windows</td>
          <td><a href="https://releases.unityide.app/latest/UnityIDESetup.exe">releases.unityide.app/latest/UnityIDESetup.exe</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>macOS (Apple silicon)</td>
          <td><a href="https://releases.unityide.app/latest/UnityIDE-arm64.dmg">releases.unityide.app/latest/UnityIDE-arm64.dmg</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Unity package</td>
          <td><a href="https://releases.unityide.app/unity-extension-releases/latest/com.unityide.editor.tgz">releases.unityide.app/unity-extension-releases/latest/com.unityide.editor.tgz</a></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    If you obtained UnityIDE anywhere else — a download portal, a mirror, a torrent,
    a bundled installer — it is not a build we published, and we cannot vouch for
    what is in it. Download it again from the links above.
  </p>

  <h2>What you get, and what you don't</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>UnityIDE is free to download and use.</strong> No payment details are
      required to install it or to work in it. Paid subscription tiers exist and
      unlock higher AI usage limits and additional model tiers; the editor itself
      does not expire.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Nothing is bundled.</strong> Our installers contain UnityIDE and
      nothing else — no toolbars, no browser extensions, no search hijacking, no
      third-party offers, no additional software presented during setup.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No hidden data collection.</strong> Exactly what we collect, and who
      else receives it, is itemised field by field in our
      <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> — including the section on AI features,
      which is explicit that your prompts and the surrounding code are sent to model
      providers.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Uninstall normally.</strong> UnityIDE removes through the standard
      uninstaller on Windows and by deleting the application on macOS. Nothing is
      left running.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Independence</h2>
  <p>
    UnityIDE is an independent product. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
    sponsored by Unity Technologies. Unity is a trademark of Unity Technologies,
    used here only to describe the engine this software is built to work with.
  </p>

  <h2 id="editorial">About our guides</h2>
  <p>
    Product guides and comparisons are written by the UnityIDE team. We identify
    the documentation used, distinguish documented capabilities from hands-on
    tests, and state the versions covered by recorded tests. Comparisons are
    published by the maker of UnityIDE; they are not independent reviews.
    Report corrections through <a href="/feedback/">our feedback form</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Elsewhere on this site</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/#download">Download UnityIDE</a> — current builds for Windows and macOS</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/">Documentation</a> — installation, the Unity package, and how the AI features work</li>
    <li><a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> — what we collect and who receives it</li>
    <li><a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> — the licence you use UnityIDE under</li>
    <li><a href="/feedback">Send feedback</a> — bugs, requests, or anything that annoyed you</li>
  </ul>
</LegalLayout>
